== Effects ==
* Grants 6 empty {{e|Bone Heart}}s.
* Removes all current {{E|Red Heart|text=Red Heart Containers}}. Does not remove existing Bone Hearts, but does empty them.
* Upon losing a Bone Heart, including ones acquired from other sources, Isaac fires a ring of 8 bones that split into more bones.
** {{dlc|nr}} Each Bone Heart lost adds a permanent +0.5 [[tears]] up.
** {{dlc|r}} Each Bone Heart lost adds a permanent +0.4 [[fire rate]], which can break the tear fire rate cap.
** Each bone does twice Isaac's damage plus a flat 22 damage; split bones do half this amount.

== Notes ==
* {{dlc+|r+}} This item has a 1% chance to drop when defeating {{e|The Frail}}.{{dlc-}}
* If Brittle Bones is removed from Isaac's inventory, its tear upgrades will not be removed but losing further Bone Hearts will no longer have an effect.
* Picking this item up as a character unable to gain Bone Hearts will grant the stats equivalent to one Bone Heart breaking.
** {{c|Keeper}} {{dlc+|r}}(and {{c|Tainted Keeper}}){{dlc-}} will also gain 24 [[Blue Fly|Blue Flies]].
* {{dlc+|r}} The tears up bonuses gained through this item will persist in the escape sequence of {{s|Mines}} II.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc|r}} Losing Bone Hearts not from taking damage (e. g. through a [[Devil Room (Item Pool)|Devil Deal]] or if a Bone Heart is replaced with a [[Broken Heart]]) will not give the tears up effect.

== Synergies ==
* {{i|Empty Vessel}}: The empty Bone Hearts will trigger Empty Vessel's effects.
* {{p|XIX - The Sun?}}: Using the card before picking up Brittle Bones allows Isaac to keep the [[heart container]]s since they will be temporarily converted to {{e|Bone Heart}}s.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|Genesis}}: Removes the tear upgrades upon use.
* {{t|Found Soul}}: The soul does not benefit from the tears up granted to Isaac. However, it will receive a fire rate increase if it somehow receives Bone Hearts and breaks them.

